<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Lord Shang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th–3rd century BCE</span> · Also known as Shangjun shu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shang-yang">Lord Shang</a> is a Chinese political text attributed to Shang Yang, the reforming minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>, though it was largely compiled by his followers in the fourth and third centuries BCE. It argues that a state grows strong by concentrating its people on farming and war, enforcing strict laws with heavy punishments and rewards, and curbing merchants and scholars. It is a founding text of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legalism">Legalism</a>.</p></div>
